    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330-a1">

                <pb facs="0595" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg501"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Prior to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Boston</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-28"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 28,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I wrote to Senator W. P. Frye, setting
                    forth in my letter the facts contained in the affidavit inclosed. He wrote me to
                    have it sworn to and to send it to you, which I have done. Will you please let
                    me know what course is best to pursue in regard to it, whether to enter a claim
                    or not? I think it is a clear, strong case, and the claim would be a just one,
                    and will be pleased to receive your advice in the matter.</p>
                <p>Yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. H. Prior.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
